WEBVTT

1
00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.700
You okay?

2
00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.000
Shit.

3
00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.500
That guy you fried
with your clever little trap?

4
00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.000
- That was our cousin.
- Cuz.

5
00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:39.300
That's Brother.
Sonny.

6
00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.700
You can call me Father.

7
00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:47.100
And you two?
You two are the kids.

8
00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.000
- What do you want?
- Speak when spoken to.

9
00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.200
Where are your scrips?

10
00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.800
No need to rush, Brother.
Let's eat first.

11
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.400
- We shouldn't linger.
- We haven't eaten in two days.

12
00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.300
This fool and his money
aren't going anywhere.

13
00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.000
He's got apples.

14
00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.000
Nobody has apples anymore.

15
00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.300
He does.

16
00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.800
Okay. All right.

17
00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:16.800
Go on.

18
00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.700
Were you brats playing doctor?

19
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.600
You touch her and you die.

20
00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:44.400
Give me your scrips.

21
00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:46.600
But hold back on me?

22
00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.600
You got five minutes.

23
00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.600
- Who are they?
- They followed you.

24
00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:04.900
No one followed me, Ren.

25
00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.400
- I made sure.
- Nobody knew I was here except you.

26
00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.900
You show up late last night,
then those guys show up?

27
00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:11.000
You found me.

28
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.000
Ren, shh.

29
00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.500
You told me to come.

30
00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.300
That's not what I meant.
It's not your fault.

31
00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:21.900
What are you doing?

32
00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.200
They had you under surveillance.
I should've known.

33
00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.300
What? Who?

34
00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:38.400
Ren, you're gonna get us killed!

35
00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:56.100
Be careful.

36
00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:07.000
- We don't have much time.
- Time for... for what?

37
00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.900
Those guys want more than just scrips.

38
00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.300
What? Ren, listen to me, okay?

39
00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.800
There's three of them,
and they've got a gun.

40
00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.000
- Do you recognize him?
- No.

41
00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.600
I think he was there
when Torus tried to arrest me.

42
00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:26.600
Don't! Don't touch it.

43
00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.200
It's rigged with 20,000 volts.

44
00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.500
It's how this guy died.

45
00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.700
- What is it?
- The ARQ.

46
00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:35.700
The ARQ?

47
00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:38.000
Arcing recursive quine.

48
00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.500
It's what they're after.

49
00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:42.100
No, they're starving like everybody else.

50
00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:46.200
So unless this thing is a food processor,
I doubt they give a shit about it.

51
00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.800
No, Torus sent those bastards
to take it back.

52
00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.100
This is what you stole from Torus?

53
00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.300
I didn't steal it.
I built it.

54
00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:58.900
What's it do?

55
00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.300
It's a hyper-efficient energy turbine.

56
00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.000
A generator. That's it?

57
00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:08.100
I know that look.

58
00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:10.800
You're not telling me something.

59
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.200
- Lock the door behind me.
- Ren.

60
00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.400
Ren, don't go.

61
00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:19.300
This door is reinforced.
It would take ZMPs to break it down.

62
00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:21.900
You're gonna get us killed.

63
00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.200
I shouldn't have contacted you, Hannah.

64
00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:27.200
Don't say that.

65
00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.800
I just needed to see you again.

66
00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:33.500
- Stay here.
- Don't go.

67
00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.900
<i>...the so-called Energy Wars,</i>

68
00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.100
<i>dominate headlines worldwide.</i>

69
00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:41.200
<i>...citizens and non-citizens celebrate</i>

70
00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:44.800
<i>the reunification of Los Angeles Island
with Torus Corporation.</i>

71
00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.900
<i>The island signed a treaty
that cedes all resources and citizens</i>

72
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.600
<i>to the conglomerate's
North American division.</i>

73
00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.500
<i>The reunification comes six days after</i>

74
00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:56.100
<i>the island's only remaining
nuclear desalination plant</i>

75
00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.900
<i>was destroyed by Bloc missiles.</i>

76
00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:01.300
Bloc drone missiles.
More Torus lies.

77
00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.400
<i>...Bloc paramilitaries
over the Great Slave Lake Oil Refinery.</i>

78
00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.400
<i>The refinery borders
the Arctic Parallel neutral zone.</i>

79
00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.700
<i>Torus executives...</i>

80
00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.000
Man, why you always gotta listen
to this propaganda, huh?

81
00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.200
Know thy enemy, my brother.

82
00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.800
Yeah, well,
the Pope tells it like it really is.

83
00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.600
<i>Those who can't remember the past</i>

84
00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.400
<i>are condemned to repeat it.</i>

85
00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:30.800
<i>Torus execs claim that the energy crisis
threatens humankind.</i>

86
00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:32.700
<i>I agree.</i>

87
00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:36.900
<i>- Torus claims to be humanity's savior...</i>
- You cut that into four pieces?

88
00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.700
- So?
- There's three of us.

89
00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:41.400
<i>...our executioner.</i>

90
00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:45.200
<i>Listen to the mad words of a wise man.</i>

91
00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:52.200
<i>"What if a demon crept after you
one night, in your loneliest...</i>

92
00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:11.100
<i>The eternal hourglass of existence
is turned upside down again and again,</i>

93
00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:12.700
<i>and you with it, too."</i>

94
00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:20.700
- Get up, Hannah.
- What? Why?

95
00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:21.900
They're coming.

96
00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.400
Who?

97
00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.600
Were you brats playing doctor?

98
00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:04.200
Touch her and you die.

99
00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:08.500
Whoa.

100
00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:10.100
So menacing.

101
00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:14.400
Give me your scrips.

102
00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.300
But hold back on me?

103
00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.900
- "You have five minutes."
- You got five minutes.

104
00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:30.400
Who the hell are they?

105
00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.500
Ren? Ren?

106
00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.800
Stop. They'll be right back.

107
00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:40.800
- We've got time.
- What?

108
00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.200
You're gonna get us killed.

109
00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:50.000
Okay. Hannah, listen to me, okay?

110
00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:52.500
Right now, this very moment,
it's happened before.

111
00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.900
Twice, I think.

112
00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.700
- What are you talking about?
- Shit.

113
00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.500
What the hell are you doing?

114
00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:03.900
Ren, you're going to get us killed.

115
00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.900
I don't want you to get hurt.

116
00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:13.400
Ren?

117
00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:19.200
Okay, listen to me. There's three of them,
and they've got a gun.

118
00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:24.500
Hannah, listen to me.

119
00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:28.100
Today is repeating.
Tell me you remember.

120
00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.500
Come on, you have to remember.

121
00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:33.700
Have you lost your fucking mind?

122
00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:36.700
- No. No.
- What?

123
00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:49.500
Incredible.

124
00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:53.000
I think... I think the ARQ
is causing time to loop.

125
00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.300
Okay, Ren, you're talking crazy.

126
00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:01.100
No. No. No, no, no.
I remember.

127
00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:05.500
Okay, this guy, um,
he's got a big scar across his face.

128
00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:12.300
Prick who calls himself Father...
Uh, brown eyes, a little bit of stubble.

129
00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:15.700
The big guy?
Brother? Dark hair, baby face.

130
00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:18.400
Sonny?
Full beard, shaved head.

131
00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:22.300
How did you know that?

132
00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:25.400
Because it's happened before.
Twice.

133
00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:29.700
Don't touch it.

134
00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.400
What else do you remember?

135
00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:38.400
Nothing...

136
00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:40.300
except that Father guy killed me.

137
00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:47.300
Well, how come you remember and I don't?

138
00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:49.600
I don't know.

139
00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.700
Oh, and what about those idiots
with the code names?

140
00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:55.900
- They don't remember either?
- Just me.

141
00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:00.200
Hannah, you don't have to believe me,
but I need you to trust me.

142
00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:05.300
<i>Torus Corporation's
global military operation</i>

143
00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:08.600
<i>against rogue states
and Bloc coalition terrorists,</i>

144
00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:12.100
<i>the so-called Energy Wars,
dominate headlines worldwide.</i>

145
00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.300
<i>On the West Coast,
citizens and non-citizens celebrate</i>

146
00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:20.700
<i>the reunification of Los Angeles Island
with Torus Corporation.</i>

147
00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.200
<i>...borders the Arctic Parallel
neutral zone.</i>

148
00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:24.300
<i>Torus executives...</i>

149
00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:27.200
Man, why you always gotta listen
to this propaganda, huh?

150
00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.300
Know thy enemy, my brother.

151
00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:32.100
Yeah, well,
the Pope tells it like it really is.

152
00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:37.700
<i>Those who can't remember the past</i>

153
00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.900
<i>are condemned to repeat it.</i>

154
00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:53.300
What are these for?

155
00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:56.700
- Cyanide gas.
- So you're gonna kill them?

156
00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:59.200
- They'll kill us first.
- You don't know that.

157
00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:00.900
They already killed me.

158
00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.300
I'm gonna crank up the thermostat.
As soon as the furnace turns on...

159
00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:04.700
Your furnace works?

160
00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:07.200
Okay, nobody has that much electricity.
Not around here.

161
00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:10.100
The ARQ powers the house.
The second the furnace turns on...

162
00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:13.900
pull this pin,
dump this canister into the chute.

163
00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.800
It feeds the entire house.
They won't be safe anywhere.

164
00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:23.700
They have masks.

165
00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.700
Air masks.
They need gas masks.

166
00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.300
You ready?

167
00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:30.300
Is it painless?

168
00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.300
It's quick.

169
00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:44.400
<i>"The eternal hourglass of existence</i>

170
00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:47.900
<i>is turned upside down again and again,</i>

171
00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.000
<i>and you with it, too.</i>

172
00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:54.400
<i>Would you not throw yourself down
and gnash your teeth,</i>

173
00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:56.500
<i>and curse the demon..."</i>

174
00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:47.500
<i>The only species left for us
to destroy is ourselves.</i>

175
00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:53.300
<i>If the Bloc and free states
don't surrender to the Torus Corporation,</i>

176
00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:59.400
<i>what happened to continental Australia
will happen to the entire planet.</i>

177
00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:02.900
<i>It will be 10,000 years</i>

178
00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:07.700
<i>before anyone can step foot
on that radioactive rubble again.</i>

179
00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.200
I'm sorry.
I couldn't do it.

180
00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.300
Mask off and lose the glove.

181
00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.000
Now.

182
00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:54.500
I wasn't lying when I said
we just wanted your scrips,

183
00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:56.700
but here you go and try and gas us.

184
00:16:56.800 --> 00:16:58.600
This kid's got a mean streak.

185
00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:01.100
- I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

186
00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.200
Hands.

187
00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:04.700
Where are your scrips?

188
00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:10.200
Just tell them.

189
00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:15.900
- I have a safe.
- See how easy that was?

190
00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:20.000
- Cooperation makes the world go round.
- And money?

191
00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.200
Where's the safe?

192
00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:52.100
Hannah, it's gonna be okay.

193
00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.900
Thirty thousand in StomaChem scrips...

194
00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:01.900
Environ, sixty-five thousand...

195
00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:06.300
Jackpot.
Over a million in Torus scrips.

196
00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:08.400
We're gonna have ourselves
a good time, boys.

197
00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:10.900
- It's for the cause, Brother.
- Yeah. Yeah, of course.

198
00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.100
But we're gonna get a finder's fee.

199
00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:15.600
You got what you came for.
Now go.

200
00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:17.400
He can identify us.

201
00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:22.200
Give me the gun.
I'll shoot him right now.

202
00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:24.800
No!

203
00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:28.700
Nobody gets hurt.

204
00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:33.900
Are you sure, Mother?

205
00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:39.600
I wasn't too rough, was I?

206
00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:42.700
He used to work for Torus.
He still might.

207
00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:47.200
We're the Bloc.

208
00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:50.600
We don't kill civilians.

209
00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:54.100
All right.
Looks like it's your lucky day, champ.

210
00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:56.500
Take anything you can hock.

211
00:18:57.100 --> 00:19:00.500
See if you can find some mask filters.
We're running out.

212
00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:10.200
The Bloc needs your scrips, Ren.

213
00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:14.700
I'd have given 'em to you.

214
00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.000
I'll be back.

215
00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.300
Hey.

216
00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:28.800
So what's that thing do anyway?
Besides fry people.

217
00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:32.100
It's just a science experiment.

218
00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:36.100
That's right. He used to be
a military engineer for Torus.

219
00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:38.100
So is that a weapon or something?

220
00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:39.700
No, it's not a...

221
00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:41.100
Jesus Christ!

222
00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:55.600
Ren?

223
00:19:57.700 --> 00:19:59.400
What the hell are you doing?

224
00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:04.300
You got five minutes.

225
00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:14.200
- Who are they?
- You don't know?

226
00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:16.800
What?

227
00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:18.300
Shh.

228
00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:20.900
Stop it! Stop it!
You're gonna get us killed.

229
00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.400
Yeah, tell me about it.

230
00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:30.400
Well, finally!

231
00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:36.500
What happened to you
after Torus tried to arrest me?

232
00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:40.000
I told you last night.

233
00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:43.000
Tell me again.

234
00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.500
Now? Why?

235
00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:48.900
Ren, untie me.

236
00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:50.900
What?

237
00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:03.400
Torus agents interrogated me
for three days.

238
00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:06.800
Then what?

239
00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:08.200
Uh, they let me go

240
00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:13.100
after they knew I had nothing to do
with you stealing their scrips.

241
00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:18.500
And that you left without telling me.

242
00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:26.200
<i>Listen carefully.
Torus... Hannah!</i>

243
00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:27.500
<i>I got this!</i>

244
00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:30.100
Ren, un... untie me.

245
00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:34.600
What is it?

246
00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:40.400
And Torus let you go?
Just like that?

247
00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:43.200
Not just like that.

248
00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:47.600
They took away my citizenship, our home.

249
00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:52.600
They put me in a refugee camp
for six months.

250
00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:58.200
I didn't know if you were dead,
or if you had just left me for dead.

251
00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:03.500
I spent a year torturing myself,

252
00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:06.300
feeling guilty that I got away
and you didn't.

253
00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:20.300
They have a gun.

254
00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:22.800
We should do what they say.

255
00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:25.200
I already tried that.

256
00:22:26.600 --> 00:22:30.000
<i>Up north, Torus
security forces battle Bloc paramilitaries</i>

257
00:22:30.100 --> 00:22:32.400
<i>over the Great Slave Lake Oil Refinery.</i>

258
00:22:32.500 --> 00:22:35.900
<i>The refinery borders
the Arctic Parallel neutral zone.</i>

259
00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.200
<i>Torus executives
accuse the Arctic Parallel</i>

260
00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:40.300
<i>of providing a safe haven
for Bloc leaders.</i>

261
00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:44.200
Man, why you always
gotta listen to this propaganda?

262
00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:46.300
Know thy enemy, my brother.

263
00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:49.000
Yeah, well,
the Pope tells it like it really is.

264
00:22:53.800 --> 00:22:57.200
<i>Those who can't remember
the past are condemned to repeat it.</i>

265
00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:11.300
Are you okay?

266
00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:15.300
Those guys hurt my back.

267
00:23:15.400 --> 00:23:17.200
There's a bag up there.
Can you reach it?

268
00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:19.200
Yeah, sure.

269
00:23:41.900 --> 00:23:43.500
My supervisors called me a fraud

270
00:23:43.500 --> 00:23:46.800
when I told them the ARQ
was generating limitless energy.

271
00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:50.600
I couldn't really blame them, though.
Perpetual motion's a myth.

272
00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:55.800
Then Torus seized the ARQ.

273
00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:58.700
Now why take something that didn't work?

274
00:23:58.800 --> 00:24:02.000
Because it does.
They want it back.

275
00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:05.100
Torus wants the ARQ for their war machine.

276
00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:08.000
You're crazy.
You've gone fucking crazy.

277
00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:10.400
Maybe.
It doesn't mean I'm wrong.

278
00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:15.100
I know everything, Hannah.

279
00:24:15.200 --> 00:24:19.500
Your boyfriend,
stealing my scrips for the Bloc...

280
00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:23.000
Mother.

281
00:24:25.900 --> 00:24:27.200
How?

282
00:24:27.300 --> 00:24:29.300
You wouldn't believe me if I told you.

283
00:24:37.300 --> 00:24:40.300
Are you really working for the Bloc,
or did Torus turn you?

284
00:24:48.300 --> 00:24:49.400
Bloc.

285
00:24:50.900 --> 00:24:52.600
We don't want your stupid machine.

286
00:24:54.600 --> 00:24:57.600
- We came for your scrips.
- Right.

287
00:24:57.700 --> 00:25:00.000
Sorry. You're a freedom fighter now.

288
00:25:00.100 --> 00:25:03.400
I'm just some fool engineer
trying to solve the world's energy crisis.

289
00:25:03.500 --> 00:25:06.000
And all this time I thought
you were just a self-serving thief.

290
00:25:06.100 --> 00:25:07.900
I don't even know who you are anymore.

291
00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:09.100
Yeah, that's right.

292
00:25:10.900 --> 00:25:12.000
You don't.

293
00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:15.400
Because you got away.

294
00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:28.100
They kept the lights on
while I tried to sleep.

295
00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:31.200
Kept me in darkness while I was awake.

296
00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:39.000
They played the same Christmas song
over and over.

297
00:25:42.700 --> 00:25:44.400
It never stopped.

298
00:25:46.200 --> 00:25:47.400
I'm sorry.

299
00:25:48.000 --> 00:25:50.200
You don't get to be sorry.

300
00:25:50.300 --> 00:25:52.800
- You're too late for sorry.
- I never...

301
00:25:52.900 --> 00:25:56.300
I never stopped thinking about you,
Hannah. I looked for you every day.

302
00:25:56.300 --> 00:25:57.800
I hacked into every database I could,

303
00:25:57.900 --> 00:26:00.900
tapped every network,
monitored every registry.

304
00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:03.700
Finding you was the only thing
that kept me going.

305
00:26:06.800 --> 00:26:08.200
I still hate you.

306
00:26:10.600 --> 00:26:11.700
Okay.

307
00:26:17.400 --> 00:26:19.000
So you're just gonna kill us now?

308
00:26:20.200 --> 00:26:22.500
- Just them.
- Ren, please.

309
00:26:23.600 --> 00:26:25.300
Nobody has to get hurt.

310
00:26:30.500 --> 00:26:31.500
We do it my way.

311
00:26:41.300 --> 00:26:43.600
<i>...what happened
to continental Australia</i>

312
00:26:43.600 --> 00:26:46.300
<i>will happen to the entire planet.</i>

313
00:26:47.800 --> 00:26:49.200
<i>It will be 10,000 years...</i>

314
00:26:49.300 --> 00:26:50.900
- Jeez.
- What the hell you doing?

315
00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:55.200
<i>...before anyone can step foot
on that radioactive rubble again.</i>

316
00:26:56.800 --> 00:26:59.000
Shoot me, we all die.

317
00:27:01.700 --> 00:27:02.800
They're bluffing.

318
00:27:12.100 --> 00:27:15.100
Hannah, baby, don't do this.
I trusted you.

319
00:27:15.200 --> 00:27:17.500
Ren's keeping half his scrips.
We get the other half.

320
00:27:17.600 --> 00:27:20.200
- Nobody gets hurt this way.
- No, wait.

321
00:27:20.300 --> 00:27:21.400
Hannah.

322
00:27:22.400 --> 00:27:24.700
Come with me.
We can start over.

323
00:27:24.800 --> 00:27:26.500
Okay? Do it right this time.
We'll head north.

324
00:27:26.600 --> 00:27:29.300
No Torus, no Bloc.
Just us.

325
00:27:31.900 --> 00:27:35.400
You should eat.
There's food in the kitchen. Just...

326
00:27:35.500 --> 00:27:37.600
Just think about it, okay?

327
00:27:41.200 --> 00:27:42.600
Hannah!

328
00:28:01.500 --> 00:28:02.500
Well...

329
00:28:03.900 --> 00:28:07.700
aren't we just one big happy family?

330
00:28:10.800 --> 00:28:12.500
You killed me.

331
00:28:17.600 --> 00:28:19.100
You punched me in the ear.

332
00:28:19.200 --> 00:28:21.200
I meant... I meant to hit you in the face.

333
00:28:21.300 --> 00:28:23.200
Huh, like this?

334
00:28:30.800 --> 00:28:33.200
Hannah's coming with me.

335
00:28:35.500 --> 00:28:36.700
Giving us your blessing?

336
00:28:39.400 --> 00:28:42.800
- She won't go with you.
- She will.

337
00:28:43.500 --> 00:28:44.800
I know Hannah.

338
00:28:44.800 --> 00:28:46.700
Then you also know that she hates you.

339
00:28:55.200 --> 00:28:56.500
Stop!

340
00:29:06.100 --> 00:29:08.400
I need a few hours
to download the data and pack up the ARQ.

341
00:29:08.500 --> 00:29:10.100
You can't go with him, Hannah.

342
00:29:10.200 --> 00:29:11.800
His mind's gone sour.

343
00:29:12.700 --> 00:29:15.300
We'll hook up with a migrant caravan,
head to the Arctic Parallel.

344
00:29:15.400 --> 00:29:17.200
I can hack weather drones
so we avoid flash...

345
00:29:17.300 --> 00:29:18.700
I can't go with you.

346
00:29:21.100 --> 00:29:22.200
I can't.

347
00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:29.200
I'm keeping my scrips.

348
00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:31.100
That wasn't the deal.

349
00:29:32.100 --> 00:29:33.200
Well, the deal's changed.

350
00:29:34.800 --> 00:29:35.900
Ren, please.

351
00:29:35.900 --> 00:29:39.100
This is bigger than us.
This is about winning the war.

352
00:29:39.200 --> 00:29:40.200
The war is over.

353
00:29:40.300 --> 00:29:42.000
Torus is gonna win.
The Bloc is doomed.

354
00:29:42.100 --> 00:29:43.800
And you are wasting your time.

355
00:29:45.200 --> 00:29:46.300
Maybe.

356
00:29:47.400 --> 00:29:48.600
But I have to try.

357
00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:55.700
We need your scrips.
All of them.

358
00:29:58.400 --> 00:29:59.400
Now!

359
00:30:00.300 --> 00:30:01.900
You're not gonna shoot me.

360
00:30:05.300 --> 00:30:06.400
You're right.

361
00:30:08.700 --> 00:30:09.800
You're just being ridiculous.

362
00:30:10.800 --> 00:30:12.800
Okay. Okay. Okay. Just...

363
00:30:24.400 --> 00:30:26.000
I shot you.

364
00:30:26.100 --> 00:30:27.600
Wait, you remember?

365
00:31:22.600 --> 00:31:24.200
Were you brats playing doctor?

366
00:31:24.300 --> 00:31:27.000
Oh, yeah.
All night long.

367
00:31:33.800 --> 00:31:35.500
Give me your scrips.

368
00:31:37.300 --> 00:31:39.000
But hold back on me?

369
00:31:49.700 --> 00:31:51.500
You got five minutes.

370
00:31:58.700 --> 00:32:01.000
You do remember.

371
00:32:02.100 --> 00:32:03.700
Is this a dream?

372
00:32:03.800 --> 00:32:06.100
It was a dream, right? Or...

373
00:32:06.200 --> 00:32:09.300
is this a dream right now? I...

374
00:32:09.300 --> 00:32:10.400
It's not a dream.

375
00:32:10.500 --> 00:32:11.800
- No.
- Today is repeating.

376
00:32:11.800 --> 00:32:15.700
No, I have to get out of here.

377
00:32:15.800 --> 00:32:19.100
- Ren, I can't. I...
- Hey. Hey. Hey. Hey. Hey. Hey.

378
00:32:19.200 --> 00:32:20.900
Everything's gonna be okay.

379
00:32:24.900 --> 00:32:26.500
How is this happening?

380
00:32:27.400 --> 00:32:28.600
The ARQ.

381
00:32:29.500 --> 00:32:31.100
How many times do you remember?

382
00:32:33.800 --> 00:32:34.900
Just one.

383
00:32:34.900 --> 00:32:37.400
But it feels like more.

384
00:32:37.400 --> 00:32:38.800
That's because it is.

385
00:32:42.400 --> 00:32:43.900
Great.

386
00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:45.600
Okay, you see these time logs?

387
00:32:45.700 --> 00:32:47.300
These are the four loops
we've gone through.

388
00:32:47.400 --> 00:32:50.700
They always begin at 6:11
and end at 9:25.

389
00:32:51.800 --> 00:32:54.700
And this last time log,
that's happening right now.

390
00:32:54.800 --> 00:32:56.500
So we've looped five times?

391
00:32:56.600 --> 00:32:58.400
- Yeah.
- How? Why?

392
00:33:01.300 --> 00:33:02.600
Okay.

393
00:33:03.400 --> 00:33:07.600
Okay, if, uh, this line is time,
this is when the loop begins.

394
00:33:07.700 --> 00:33:12.000
At 6:11 a.m.,
Cuz electrocuted himself on the ARQ.

395
00:33:12.100 --> 00:33:14.700
This caused forward time
to bend back on itself,

396
00:33:14.700 --> 00:33:16.700
creating a closed-time loop.

397
00:33:19.200 --> 00:33:20.600
And the day repeats.

398
00:33:20.700 --> 00:33:24.600
Time resets every three hours,
14 minutes and 15 seconds.

399
00:33:28.100 --> 00:33:29.600
How does the ARQ work?

400
00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:32.200
Um... Okay.

401
00:33:32.300 --> 00:33:35.200
I mean... I mean, essentially,
these fuel cells power the ARQ.

402
00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:39.300
In turn, the ARQ recharges the fuel cells.

403
00:33:39.300 --> 00:33:42.200
It never needs an external power source,

404
00:33:42.300 --> 00:33:44.900
but... how it's looping time,
I have no idea.

405
00:33:45.700 --> 00:33:49.000
An unlimited energy machine

406
00:33:49.100 --> 00:33:52.100
that also produces unlimited time?

407
00:33:52.200 --> 00:33:53.700
No wonder Torus wants it back.

408
00:33:53.800 --> 00:33:56.200
Not unlimited time.
The same amount of time over and over.

409
00:33:57.000 --> 00:34:00.200
The loops always reset at 9:25.

410
00:34:00.300 --> 00:34:02.200
What happened
when the previous loop reset,

411
00:34:02.300 --> 00:34:04.600
shortly after you shot me?

412
00:34:04.700 --> 00:34:06.700
- It was an accident.
- What happened?

413
00:34:06.800 --> 00:34:09.900
I untied everyone, uh, a gun went off,

414
00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:12.500
and then I woke up in bed next to you.
That's it. That's all I remember.

415
00:34:12.600 --> 00:34:13.800
Sonny probably shot you.

416
00:34:14.700 --> 00:34:16.200
Or maybe your boyfriend.

417
00:34:16.300 --> 00:34:17.800
Grimm wouldn't do that.

418
00:34:19.900 --> 00:34:21.000
Do you love him?

419
00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:25.800
Grimm was the one who helped me survive.

420
00:34:26.700 --> 00:34:28.200
I owe him.

421
00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:31.700
So he's the reason
you joined up with the Bloc?

422
00:34:32.600 --> 00:34:35.600
Five months in Torus custody
was pretty convincing.

423
00:34:38.800 --> 00:34:40.700
Ren, it was my idea to rob you.

424
00:34:42.400 --> 00:34:43.800
I was angry.

425
00:34:47.800 --> 00:34:49.300
But I also wanted to see you.

426
00:34:51.300 --> 00:34:53.500
To make sure you were okay.
That's the truth.

427
00:34:56.800 --> 00:34:58.900
Hannah, just come with me.

428
00:34:59.000 --> 00:35:02.000
Ren, there is a war on.
You come with me.

429
00:35:02.100 --> 00:35:04.100
Oh, my God.
To the Bloc? Come on.

430
00:35:04.200 --> 00:35:06.600
You say you wanna solve
the world's energy crisis,

431
00:35:06.600 --> 00:35:08.800
- but you just wanna run away.
- Yes, with you.

432
00:35:08.900 --> 00:35:11.300
No, it's time we end this.

433
00:35:13.200 --> 00:35:15.000
Fine. Fine.

434
00:35:15.100 --> 00:35:17.300
- Fine, shut down the ARQ.
- No.

435
00:35:18.200 --> 00:35:20.100
No, not until we're in control.

436
00:35:20.200 --> 00:35:22.800
If we shut down the ARQ
and Sonny kills either one of us...

437
00:35:22.900 --> 00:35:25.700
- We're dead for good.
- Which is why we need to kill them first.

438
00:35:25.800 --> 00:35:28.400
No. They're not murderers.

439
00:35:28.500 --> 00:35:30.500
Sonny is. He will shoot me.
That's how it plays out.

440
00:35:30.500 --> 00:35:32.700
Then I will make sure that he can't.

441
00:35:32.800 --> 00:35:35.600
They're my subordinates.
Ren, they will do what I say.

442
00:35:35.700 --> 00:35:36.800
Even Sonny?

443
00:35:37.400 --> 00:35:41.100
Ren, please.
I don't want anybody else to get hurt.

444
00:35:44.000 --> 00:35:45.800
This is gonna work.

445
00:35:45.800 --> 00:35:47.800
Just not too tight, okay?

446
00:35:48.800 --> 00:35:50.100
Trust me.

447
00:36:09.300 --> 00:36:12.100
Hey, guys!
Get in here!

448
00:36:17.700 --> 00:36:19.000
What's going on?

449
00:36:19.100 --> 00:36:20.800
I know where his scrips are.

450
00:36:22.300 --> 00:36:23.400
Untie me.

451
00:36:26.900 --> 00:36:28.500
That was easy.

452
00:36:28.600 --> 00:36:30.300
Does he have any more apples?

453
00:36:35.400 --> 00:36:37.700
So you broke cover?

454
00:36:37.800 --> 00:36:40.100
Betraying me for money?
You're pathetic.

455
00:36:43.900 --> 00:36:45.300
I want him to know the truth.

456
00:36:47.800 --> 00:36:49.300
Say cheese, bud.

457
00:36:58.300 --> 00:36:59.400
Check 'em.

458
00:37:00.500 --> 00:37:04.000
All right, let's move. I don't wanna
be stuck in Torus territory after dark.

459
00:37:05.900 --> 00:37:07.100
What about lover boy?

460
00:37:07.100 --> 00:37:08.700
He's seen our faces.

461
00:37:08.800 --> 00:37:10.200
No, he won't say anything.

462
00:37:13.000 --> 00:37:14.100
I guess it's your lucky day, champ.

463
00:37:15.400 --> 00:37:18.900
Everyone search.
Take anything we can hock.

464
00:37:19.000 --> 00:37:21.900
And look for air mask filters.
We're running low.

465
00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:37.700
What about the Cuz killer?

466
00:37:37.800 --> 00:37:39.400
We could probably strip it for parts?

467
00:37:40.500 --> 00:37:41.900
Hey, genius.

468
00:37:42.000 --> 00:37:43.900
What's that thing do anyway,
besides fry people?

469
00:37:49.400 --> 00:37:53.400
That's right.
You were a military engineer at Torus.

470
00:37:53.500 --> 00:37:55.700
So that's why it's
like a weapon or something?

471
00:37:56.900 --> 00:37:58.100
We're taking it with us.

472
00:38:03.100 --> 00:38:04.500
What's it do?

473
00:38:04.600 --> 00:38:06.800
We'll find a use for it.

474
00:38:06.900 --> 00:38:11.100
Listen to me, Ren.
I'm sorry, but it has to be this way.

475
00:38:26.600 --> 00:38:28.600
She didn't tie your legs back up.

476
00:38:33.600 --> 00:38:36.000
Do you know you're still on Torus payroll?

477
00:38:39.100 --> 00:38:40.900
Torus didn't want word getting out
that you disappeared

478
00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:42.900
with their most valuable possession.

479
00:38:43.900 --> 00:38:45.500
Whatever the hell that is.

480
00:38:47.200 --> 00:38:49.000
What's that thing run on, anyway?

481
00:38:50.700 --> 00:38:51.700
Love.

482
00:38:53.400 --> 00:38:56.600
My grams always used to say
that love made the world go round.

483
00:38:57.500 --> 00:39:00.200
But then, she was sick in the head
with the kuru virus, so...

484
00:39:10.700 --> 00:39:11.800
Mobius Common.

485
00:39:13.100 --> 00:39:15.100
<i>Identify yourself.</i>

486
00:39:15.200 --> 00:39:17.200
Ouroboros forty-six clear niner-four.

487
00:39:17.300 --> 00:39:21.000
Request recon crush-down
for Operation Riverrun. Over.

488
00:39:21.100 --> 00:39:24.100
<i>Triangulating coordinates.
Stand by.</i>

489
00:39:26.100 --> 00:39:28.400
<i>ZMP fiver-Delta is in proximity.</i>

490
00:39:29.400 --> 00:39:30.800
<i>Drop time imminent.</i>

491
00:39:30.900 --> 00:39:32.200
Copy. Out.

492
00:39:35.300 --> 00:39:37.300
Did Torus promise your freedom
if you found me?

493
00:39:38.200 --> 00:39:40.100
You know they're lying, but I can help.

494
00:39:41.300 --> 00:39:43.100
Is that the best you got?

495
00:39:43.200 --> 00:39:45.100
Oh.

496
00:39:45.200 --> 00:39:48.400
That'll smart.
How do I disable it?

497
00:39:52.800 --> 00:39:54.000
I use that?

498
00:39:55.600 --> 00:39:56.600
What's the login?

499
00:40:00.800 --> 00:40:02.800
What's the login?

500
00:40:06.500 --> 00:40:07.500
Hannah.

501
00:40:08.800 --> 00:40:10.800
Hannah?
Seriously?

502
00:40:12.700 --> 00:40:14.500
Well, I guess that's romantic.

503
00:40:25.200 --> 00:40:28.700
I get paid whether I bring you back
dead or alive.

504
00:40:28.800 --> 00:40:30.000
What's the login?

505
00:40:37.400 --> 00:40:39.600
You're running out of time.

506
00:40:40.500 --> 00:40:41.600
Is that the best you...

507
00:40:43.300 --> 00:40:45.400
Hannah, wake up.

508
00:40:47.000 --> 00:40:48.100
Sonny shot me.

509
00:40:48.200 --> 00:40:50.800
- Sonny's a merc. Torus sent him.
- Torus?

510
00:40:51.800 --> 00:40:53.100
What do we do?

511
00:40:53.700 --> 00:40:55.700
Play along.

512
00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:08.500
Did he just say "play along"?

513
00:41:08.600 --> 00:41:10.700
I don't know.
I was asleep.

514
00:41:10.800 --> 00:41:13.300
You idiots scared the shit out of me.
You're four hours early.

515
00:41:13.400 --> 00:41:14.400
Cuz is dead.

516
00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:17.200
He got electrocuted
by some crazy machine in the garage.

517
00:41:19.600 --> 00:41:20.900
Grimm.

518
00:41:25.400 --> 00:41:27.400
- Did you fuck him?
- No.

519
00:41:29.200 --> 00:41:30.600
The plan, remember?

520
00:41:30.600 --> 00:41:32.700
- Get Renton to let his guard down.
- Yeah, but not your guard.

521
00:41:32.800 --> 00:41:33.900
Stop it.

522
00:41:36.100 --> 00:41:38.300
We fell asleep after talking all night.

523
00:41:39.200 --> 00:41:40.400
That's it.

524
00:41:41.300 --> 00:41:43.600
Then... what?

525
00:41:44.800 --> 00:41:46.500
Give me five minutes alone with Renton.

526
00:41:48.300 --> 00:41:51.600
Leave you two alone together?
Yeah, that won't look at all suspicious.

527
00:41:51.700 --> 00:41:55.000
Just go to the kitchen and eat.
That's believable.

528
00:41:55.100 --> 00:41:56.800
We're not here to eat.

529
00:41:58.000 --> 00:41:59.600
He has apples.

530
00:42:00.400 --> 00:42:02.200
Nobody has apples anymore.

531
00:42:02.300 --> 00:42:03.600
He does.

532
00:42:04.800 --> 00:42:06.200
Okay. All right.

533
00:42:11.600 --> 00:42:12.700
Go on.

534
00:42:32.200 --> 00:42:33.900
Were you brats playing doctor?

535
00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:35.200
Just leave us alone.

536
00:42:40.500 --> 00:42:41.900
Give me your scrips.

537
00:42:42.800 --> 00:42:44.300
You got five minutes.

538
00:42:47.500 --> 00:42:49.100
You're not taking the ARQ.

539
00:42:53.100 --> 00:42:55.900
We need to tell Grimm about Sonny.

540
00:42:57.900 --> 00:42:59.700
I don't trust him.

541
00:42:59.800 --> 00:43:01.900
I don't even trust you right now.

542
00:43:03.000 --> 00:43:06.000
Renton, if Sonny's a merc,
we need all the help we can get.

543
00:43:09.400 --> 00:43:12.100
<i>The air is too toxic to breathe.</i>

544
00:43:13.200 --> 00:43:16.700
<i>Our water, a poisonous ink.</i>

545
00:43:16.800 --> 00:43:19.100
<i>Summer is cold. Winter's hot.</i>

546
00:43:20.300 --> 00:43:23.300
<i>And now that the birds are extinct,</i>

547
00:43:23.300 --> 00:43:24.800
<i>the only species left...</i>

548
00:43:24.900 --> 00:43:26.500
You know, I heard this broadcast before.

549
00:43:28.400 --> 00:43:31.400
- Must be a repeat.
- That's because Torus have her.

550
00:43:33.100 --> 00:43:34.800
You got a real negative attitude,
you know that?

551
00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:38.300
<i>...what happened
to continental Australia</i>

552
00:43:38.400 --> 00:43:40.900
<i>will happen to the entire planet.</i>

553
00:43:42.700 --> 00:43:45.900
<i>It will be 10,000 years</i>

554
00:43:45.900 --> 00:43:50.300
<i>before anyone can step foot
on that radioactive rubble again.</i>

555
00:43:50.300 --> 00:43:51.600
What's that?

556
00:43:51.700 --> 00:43:52.700
Kerosene.

557
00:43:53.700 --> 00:43:54.900
It's ours now.

558
00:43:55.400 --> 00:43:58.200
<i>Torus will plunder.</i>

559
00:43:58.300 --> 00:44:02.900
<i>The company will consume
until there's nothing left to consume.</i>

560
00:44:04.000 --> 00:44:07.100
<i>Torus claims they're humanity's savior.</i>

561
00:44:07.200 --> 00:44:11.800
<i>Take them true for what they really are,
our executioner.</i>

562
00:44:12.800 --> 00:44:14.300
You cut that into four pieces?

563
00:44:15.700 --> 00:44:16.700
So?

564
00:44:16.800 --> 00:44:18.900
So there's three of us.

565
00:44:19.000 --> 00:44:21.600
- Yeah, well, Hannah makes four.
- Oh, don't say her name, dummy.

566
00:44:36.100 --> 00:44:37.200
Where'd he go?

567
00:44:40.700 --> 00:44:42.300
God!

568
00:44:42.400 --> 00:44:44.500
He escaped while you idiots
were stuffing your faces.

569
00:44:44.600 --> 00:44:46.900
- It was your idea.
- Yeah, well, you took too long.

570
00:44:47.000 --> 00:44:48.800
He's probably long gone.
The scrips, too.

571
00:44:48.900 --> 00:44:51.800
- Nah, he's still in the house.
- How do you know?

572
00:44:51.900 --> 00:44:53.000
Hunch.

573
00:44:55.300 --> 00:44:58.400
You two search the main floor.
Me and Grimm will take the basement. Go.

574
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:02.300
- We should stick together.
- Go.

575
00:45:12.400 --> 00:45:14.900
- What are you doing?
- We need to kill Sonny.

576
00:45:16.400 --> 00:45:17.800
Sonny?

577
00:45:19.600 --> 00:45:20.700
Sonny?

578
00:45:56.100 --> 00:45:57.300
Don't look at me like that.

579
00:45:57.400 --> 00:45:59.100
Why would Torus care about
a few thousand scrips?

580
00:45:59.200 --> 00:46:02.500
No, they don't care about the money.
They care about this.

581
00:46:03.600 --> 00:46:05.200
What's special about this thing?

582
00:46:06.100 --> 00:46:07.600
It's a time machine.

583
00:48:12.100 --> 00:48:15.200
At 6:11, Cuz was electrocuted,

584
00:48:15.300 --> 00:48:18.700
which shorted the ARQ
and caused time to loop.

585
00:48:19.600 --> 00:48:21.800
- A time loop?
- Yes.

586
00:48:21.900 --> 00:48:24.300
And Torus sent Sonny to take the ARQ back.

587
00:48:27.100 --> 00:48:30.500
- Hannah, Sonny's a friend.
- Some friend.

588
00:48:31.200 --> 00:48:34.100
He's already killed you once.
Probably more.

589
00:48:49.300 --> 00:48:50.900
Did you find him?

590
00:48:51.000 --> 00:48:54.800
No... but he killed Brother.

591
00:48:54.900 --> 00:48:56.500
He's lying.

592
00:48:59.000 --> 00:49:00.500
Where'd you get that?

593
00:49:04.300 --> 00:49:06.700
- Where is he?
- He's gone.

594
00:49:07.600 --> 00:49:09.100
Aw, and he left you here all alone?

595
00:49:09.800 --> 00:49:12.400
No. Renton only cares about himself.

596
00:49:12.500 --> 00:49:14.100
And the ARQ.

597
00:49:33.700 --> 00:49:35.200
Is it over?

598
00:49:46.300 --> 00:49:48.200
Let's shut this damn thing down.

599
00:49:50.100 --> 00:49:52.300
Is the ARQ spinning faster?

600
00:49:52.300 --> 00:49:53.900
I have no idea.

601
00:50:08.100 --> 00:50:09.600
September 19th.

602
00:50:18.500 --> 00:50:20.500
That was the last time we saw each other.

603
00:50:23.700 --> 00:50:26.400
If I could relive one day,

604
00:50:26.500 --> 00:50:27.800
I'd...

605
00:50:33.700 --> 00:50:35.300
Grimm.

606
00:50:35.400 --> 00:50:36.600
Oh, my God. He's alive.

607
00:50:36.600 --> 00:50:39.800
Grimm. Grimm, look at me.
Look at me. You're gonna be okay.

608
00:50:39.900 --> 00:50:42.000
Get a first aid kit or something!

609
00:50:42.100 --> 00:50:43.200
Okay.

610
00:51:05.300 --> 00:51:06.500
Fuck!

611
00:51:09.900 --> 00:51:11.200
Oh, fuck!

612
00:51:14.500 --> 00:51:16.700
- What are you doing?
- Stand back.

613
00:51:16.800 --> 00:51:18.400
We don't have air masks.

614
00:52:11.100 --> 00:52:13.900
- Why is this loop different?
- Sonny's aware of the time loops.

615
00:52:14.800 --> 00:52:18.400
- Sonny's aware, how?
- I don't know. How did you become aware?

616
00:52:18.400 --> 00:52:20.400
- I just woke up and remembered.
- Me, too.

617
00:52:23.800 --> 00:52:26.700
- So is remembering just random?
- No.

618
00:52:26.800 --> 00:52:27.800
No, no, no, no.

619
00:52:27.900 --> 00:52:31.400
The ARQ emits electromagnetic frequencies
that could affect memory.

620
00:52:32.400 --> 00:52:35.700
We're farthest away from the ARQ
when it resets.

621
00:52:35.800 --> 00:52:39.300
Yeah, which is why
the effect wore off on us first.

622
00:52:40.600 --> 00:52:42.200
And now Sonny. Shit.

623
00:52:46.900 --> 00:52:48.500
Data's still the same.

624
00:52:49.700 --> 00:52:52.700
Loops begin and end at the same time.
Then everything resets.

625
00:52:54.000 --> 00:52:55.800
Why doesn't the data also reset?

626
00:52:59.100 --> 00:53:02.300
The time logs are housed
in the ARQ's core structure, above the...

627
00:53:03.700 --> 00:53:04.800
fuel cells.

628
00:53:07.100 --> 00:53:10.500
The loop ends at 9:25 'cause that's
when the power source runs out.

629
00:53:10.600 --> 00:53:13.000
When the... the fuel cells go dead?

630
00:53:13.500 --> 00:53:15.600
When the loop resets,
the fuel cells are still charged.

631
00:53:15.700 --> 00:53:20.200
The ARQ isn't producing unlimited energy.
It's just using the same energy.

632
00:53:28.100 --> 00:53:30.100
Okay, that's great, but what about Sonny?

633
00:53:34.900 --> 00:53:36.400
Shit.

634
00:53:36.500 --> 00:53:38.200
We stop Sonny
before he calls in the ZMPs.

635
00:53:52.700 --> 00:53:54.000
No sign of Sonny.

636
00:54:00.500 --> 00:54:02.400
We should go while we have the chance.

637
00:54:04.400 --> 00:54:06.600
- And take the ARQ to the Bloc.
- Oh, come on.

638
00:54:06.700 --> 00:54:08.100
- Just hear me out.
- No.

639
00:54:08.100 --> 00:54:09.900
Any battle the Bloc loses with the ARQ,

640
00:54:10.000 --> 00:54:12.600
they'll be able to loop back in time
and fight again...

641
00:54:13.500 --> 00:54:16.300
until they get it right, until we win.

642
00:54:16.400 --> 00:54:17.900
- You don't know that.
- Neither do you.

643
00:54:17.900 --> 00:54:20.100
But if Torus gets the ARQ...

644
00:54:21.500 --> 00:54:22.700
they'll be unstoppable.

645
00:54:22.700 --> 00:54:25.800
Torus can't get the ARQ,
but neither can the Bloc.

646
00:54:26.700 --> 00:54:28.900
You would rather keep it to yourself.

647
00:54:30.300 --> 00:54:32.300
You haven't changed.

648
00:54:32.400 --> 00:54:34.200
- Still selfish and...
- I'm selfish?

649
00:54:34.300 --> 00:54:37.800
All I care about is you.
All you care about is the Bloc.

650
00:54:37.900 --> 00:54:41.500
Ren, there is a war on.
I don't have time for us.

651
00:54:43.200 --> 00:54:44.800
Then what are you fighting for?

652
00:54:48.600 --> 00:54:52.100
The ARQ is dangerous in the wrong hands.
I don't trust the Bloc.

653
00:54:53.100 --> 00:54:54.500
Then trust me.

654
00:54:57.200 --> 00:55:00.900
Look, if Sonny gets me before I get him...

655
00:55:00.900 --> 00:55:02.700
He won't.

656
00:55:02.800 --> 00:55:05.700
You can't let him take the ARQ.
You have to destroy it.

657
00:55:07.300 --> 00:55:08.700
How?

658
00:55:09.300 --> 00:55:12.200
Enter the self-destruct prompt
into the user ID.

659
00:55:12.300 --> 00:55:14.200
It'll wipe the system,
melt the circuit boards,

660
00:55:14.300 --> 00:55:15.600
the cylinder will spin out of control.

661
00:55:15.700 --> 00:55:17.700
Everything will be lost.

662
00:55:19.800 --> 00:55:21.200
What's the prompt?

663
00:55:21.900 --> 00:55:24.500
- This is a last resort.
- I know.

664
00:55:26.000 --> 00:55:27.300
What's the prompt?

665
00:55:31.100 --> 00:55:33.700
Just before we were separated,
I gave you a code word.

666
00:55:35.600 --> 00:55:38.500
- You mean before you left me.
- Do you remember?

667
00:55:40.400 --> 00:55:41.900
I remember you acting paranoid.

668
00:55:42.000 --> 00:55:44.800
Hannah, I was trying to warn you.

669
00:55:52.000 --> 00:55:53.100
Sky.

670
00:58:29.500 --> 00:58:31.200
Hannah, open the door!

671
00:58:31.200 --> 00:58:32.800
Hannah!

672
00:58:54.600 --> 00:58:56.300
You checked the wrong pocket.

673
00:58:57.200 --> 00:58:59.900
- Mobius Common.
<i>- Identify yourself.</i>

674
00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:01.000
- You okay?
- Yeah.

675
00:59:01.100 --> 00:59:02.700
Ouroboros forty-six
clear niner-four.

676
00:59:02.800 --> 00:59:05.600
Request recon crush-down
for Operation Riverrun. Over.

677
00:59:06.600 --> 00:59:08.100
<i>Triangulating coordinates.</i>

678
00:59:09.600 --> 00:59:12.200
- You don't know what you're doing.
- Oh, you got that right.

679
00:59:12.300 --> 00:59:14.300
I was ordered
to recover an energy turbine.

680
00:59:14.400 --> 00:59:16.500
Apparently, it's a time machine.

681
00:59:16.600 --> 00:59:18.700
<i>ZMP fiver-Delta is in proximity.</i>

682
00:59:19.700 --> 00:59:21.200
<i>Drop time imminent.</i>

683
00:59:21.200 --> 00:59:22.600
Copy. Out.

684
00:59:23.400 --> 00:59:26.700
You're nothing to Torus.
An expendable pawn.

685
00:59:26.800 --> 00:59:28.500
Like you are to the Bloc?

686
00:59:28.600 --> 00:59:32.600
If Torus gets the ARQ, they'll kill
millions more than they already have.

687
00:59:32.700 --> 00:59:35.100
People have been killing each other
since the dawn of time.

688
00:59:35.200 --> 00:59:37.900
Yeah.
Because of people like you.

689
00:59:38.000 --> 00:59:39.700
You misunderstand me.

690
00:59:39.800 --> 00:59:42.500
This war kills us all.
I don't want that.

691
00:59:42.600 --> 00:59:45.500
So you're giving the ARQ
to the bastards who started the war.

692
00:59:46.500 --> 00:59:48.700
Better that someone wins
than everybody dies.

693
00:59:49.500 --> 00:59:51.100
What's the login?

694
00:59:55.900 --> 00:59:56.900
Sky.

695
00:59:59.900 --> 01:00:01.200
Sky.

696
01:00:07.700 --> 01:00:09.800
We've been here before.
How does it end?

697
01:00:11.800 --> 01:00:13.200
You shoot me in the face.

698
01:00:13.300 --> 01:00:16.300
- Well, I guess history does repeat.
- Okay. Okay.

699
01:00:17.200 --> 01:00:18.400
Just...

700
01:00:19.500 --> 01:00:20.700
I'll shut it down.

701
01:00:28.900 --> 01:00:31.100
Why didn't you destroy the ARQ?

702
01:00:33.100 --> 01:00:35.600
We need help.
We need to tell Grimm.

703
01:00:35.700 --> 01:00:37.500
- We tried that. It didn't work.
- We try again.

704
01:00:37.600 --> 01:00:39.700
Do the same thing,
expect different results?

705
01:00:39.800 --> 01:00:41.400
Do you have a better idea?

706
01:01:25.000 --> 01:01:27.700
Hey, he wasn't moving
for a second. It was crazy.

707
01:01:32.600 --> 01:01:34.700
Sonny saved your life, man.

708
01:01:34.800 --> 01:01:38.000
You were being electrocuted, dude.
You were like...

709
01:01:38.000 --> 01:01:39.400
He was crazy.
He didn't hesitate.

710
01:01:39.500 --> 01:01:42.300
He just jumped in, kicked you off.
Now you're back.

711
01:01:42.400 --> 01:01:44.000
You all right?

712
01:01:44.100 --> 01:01:46.200
Just déjà vu.

713
01:02:01.500 --> 01:02:03.100
All right, change of plans?

714
01:02:03.200 --> 01:02:04.200
This is it.

715
01:02:05.300 --> 01:02:07.600
What about the target?
Is he here?

716
01:02:07.700 --> 01:02:10.400
We gotta disable that
before we take him down.

717
01:02:10.500 --> 01:02:11.500
Why?

718
01:02:44.600 --> 01:02:46.200
How well do you know that Cuz guy?

719
01:02:46.300 --> 01:02:50.000
I don't. He's Sonny's guy.
He's quiet. He didn't say much.

720
01:02:51.100 --> 01:02:52.800
You're sure this is safe?

721
01:02:54.100 --> 01:02:55.500
- Ready?
- Yeah.

722
01:03:18.800 --> 01:03:19.900
Almonds?

723
01:03:27.500 --> 01:03:28.600
Cyanide.

724
01:04:11.100 --> 01:04:12.700
The ARQ is speeding up.

725
01:04:14.000 --> 01:04:16.400
The faster it spins,
the faster time moves.

726
01:04:31.700 --> 01:04:33.200
Why are we doing this?

727
01:04:40.900 --> 01:04:42.000
Don't be mad now.

728
01:04:48.000 --> 01:04:50.700
They'll die before the ARQ resets.

729
01:04:50.800 --> 01:04:52.200
Okay? It'll work.

730
01:04:54.900 --> 01:04:59.100
In the last loop, before the ARQ reset...

731
01:05:01.800 --> 01:05:03.900
What? What happened?

732
01:05:05.200 --> 01:05:07.400
It's not as if something happened...

733
01:05:08.700 --> 01:05:11.200
it's more that everything
stopped happening.

734
01:05:13.200 --> 01:05:14.500
Hannah, the ARQ is dangerous.

735
01:05:15.400 --> 01:05:17.200
You should have destroyed it.

736
01:05:19.800 --> 01:05:20.800
And let you die?

737
01:05:52.900 --> 01:05:54.100
It's safe.

738
01:05:58.600 --> 01:05:59.600
Cyanide did this?

739
01:05:59.700 --> 01:06:02.200
No. Sonny did this.

740
01:06:05.600 --> 01:06:07.300
Were the loops making him crazy?

741
01:06:07.400 --> 01:06:10.700
No. No, he probably did this
just to slow us down.

742
01:06:10.800 --> 01:06:12.500
Because ZMPs are coming.
We gotta move.

743
01:06:12.600 --> 01:06:15.600
Okay, I'll download the data
and dismantle the ARQ.

744
01:06:15.700 --> 01:06:17.100
And take it to the Bloc.

745
01:06:17.100 --> 01:06:20.200
- Hannah, not this shit!
- Ren, wha...

746
01:06:20.300 --> 01:06:21.900
We can end the war.

747
01:06:21.900 --> 01:06:24.500
What? A few rebels defeating
the largest corporation on Earth?

748
01:06:24.600 --> 01:06:26.200
Yes, it can happen.

749
01:06:26.300 --> 01:06:30.100
Torus has standing armies, okay?
Fighter drones, ZMPs, fucking nukes!

750
01:06:30.200 --> 01:06:31.800
And the Bloc would have the ARQ.

751
01:06:32.600 --> 01:06:34.800
- Forever the idealist.
- Forever the pessimist.

752
01:06:34.900 --> 01:06:37.200
Realist, okay? Evidence and facts,
not wishful thinking.

753
01:06:37.300 --> 01:06:39.600
- I call it hope.
- When did you become so naive?

754
01:06:39.700 --> 01:06:42.000
Oh, God damn it!
Fuck you!

755
01:06:45.600 --> 01:06:46.700
Oh, my God.

756
01:06:46.800 --> 01:06:47.800
What?

757
01:06:48.900 --> 01:06:49.900
Ren?

758
01:06:56.500 --> 01:06:57.700
Look.

759
01:06:57.800 --> 01:06:59.600
<i>Listen carefully. Torus... Hannah!</i>

760
01:07:03.300 --> 01:07:04.500
<i>Torus...</i>

761
01:07:05.600 --> 01:07:07.600
- I don't remember that.
- Neither do I.

762
01:07:08.800 --> 01:07:11.200
This was recorded
just before the loop resets.

763
01:07:17.400 --> 01:07:18.600
The crack.

764
01:07:20.300 --> 01:07:21.600
It's different.

765
01:07:23.000 --> 01:07:25.100
- What does it mean?
- I don't know.

766
01:07:27.800 --> 01:07:28.800
Oh, shit!

767
01:07:31.000 --> 01:07:32.500
ZMPs.

768
01:07:33.100 --> 01:07:34.400
- We gotta get out of here.
- Okay. Okay.

769
01:07:34.500 --> 01:07:36.300
- Grab scrips, supplies...
- Yep.

770
01:07:36.400 --> 01:07:37.900
I'll lock it down.

771
01:07:41.300 --> 01:07:42.900
There's something in his mouth.

772
01:08:23.900 --> 01:08:25.200
Our code word.

773
01:08:26.600 --> 01:08:28.500
- What?
- Sky.

774
01:08:28.600 --> 01:08:30.800
No! Hannah, don't move!

775
01:08:30.900 --> 01:08:33.000
No! No. Shit!

776
01:08:33.900 --> 01:08:38.100
No. No.
No. No. No. Fuck.

777
01:08:39.500 --> 01:08:40.600
Come on, Hannah.

778
01:08:44.100 --> 01:08:47.200
Hannah, come on, breathe.
Breathe.

779
01:08:48.400 --> 01:08:49.500
Hannah.

780
01:08:50.500 --> 01:08:53.100
Hannah, come on.
Come on.

781
01:10:00.200 --> 01:10:01.200
Come here.

782
01:10:02.200 --> 01:10:03.200
Come on.

783
01:10:36.800 --> 01:10:37.900
Hey.

784
01:10:38.000 --> 01:10:39.700
Hey. Hey.

785
01:10:39.800 --> 01:10:40.800
You okay?

786
01:10:40.900 --> 01:10:41.900
What happened?

787
01:10:44.200 --> 01:10:47.500
I'm sorry about what I said.
I was wrong.

788
01:10:51.600 --> 01:10:53.800
It's okay.

789
01:10:55.200 --> 01:10:57.300
Stop! Stop.

790
01:10:57.400 --> 01:10:59.000
What? No, don't!

791
01:10:59.500 --> 01:11:00.600
Where's Sonny?

792
01:11:02.000 --> 01:11:03.700
Where is he?

793
01:11:03.800 --> 01:11:05.200
There goes the plan.

794
01:11:05.300 --> 01:11:07.800
Sonny just stopped Cuz
from being electrocuted, didn't he?

795
01:11:08.800 --> 01:11:10.000
Did you tell him?

796
01:11:11.600 --> 01:11:12.800
No. Well...

797
01:11:12.900 --> 01:11:14.400
sort of.

798
01:11:14.500 --> 01:11:17.300
- What's that mean?
- Sonny and Cuz are mercs.

799
01:11:17.400 --> 01:11:18.500
Come on.

800
01:11:18.600 --> 01:11:22.400
Torus sent him.
They want Renton's machine.

801
01:11:22.400 --> 01:11:24.800
- That thing in the garage?
- Yes.

802
01:11:24.900 --> 01:11:26.200
What about it?

803
01:11:29.900 --> 01:11:31.400
It loops time.

804
01:11:32.300 --> 01:11:34.700
We've been reliving the same day
over and over.

805
01:11:34.700 --> 01:11:35.800
Oh, brother!

806
01:11:36.600 --> 01:11:38.800
If you don't help us, we're all gonna die.

807
01:11:38.800 --> 01:11:40.500
Us? Liar.

808
01:11:41.100 --> 01:11:43.600
No!

809
01:11:44.200 --> 01:11:45.400
I remember.

810
01:11:46.100 --> 01:11:47.500
Prove it.

811
01:11:48.100 --> 01:11:51.300
Grimm, what do you remember?

812
01:11:51.400 --> 01:11:53.100
I had a déjà vu and Sonny shot me.

813
01:11:54.100 --> 01:11:56.000
- Then you, too.
- Right.

814
01:12:02.400 --> 01:12:04.700
- So this is for real?
- Yes.

815
01:12:07.100 --> 01:12:08.400
You gonna help us?

816
01:12:15.100 --> 01:12:16.400
What do we do?

817
01:12:17.800 --> 01:12:19.600
You all are sick with the kuru virus,
you know that?

818
01:12:19.700 --> 01:12:20.700
Quiet.

819
01:12:22.000 --> 01:12:24.100
Sonny shot you because you were aware.

820
01:12:24.200 --> 01:12:25.300
So?

821
01:12:25.400 --> 01:12:28.400
If he knew you were aware,
why would he send you to get us?

822
01:12:28.500 --> 01:12:30.800
Sonny would expect him to betray him.

823
01:12:30.800 --> 01:12:31.800
What?

824
01:12:36.600 --> 01:12:37.800
You two really are mercs.

825
01:12:43.500 --> 01:12:44.800
Go on. Kneel down.

826
01:12:45.900 --> 01:12:47.200
Kneel down!

827
01:12:48.600 --> 01:12:49.800
Kneel down.

828
01:12:50.700 --> 01:12:52.700
Down on your...
No. No, not you.

829
01:12:56.800 --> 01:12:59.300
Everyone kneel but you.
You sit down.

830
01:13:02.100 --> 01:13:03.700
Go to hell.

831
01:13:14.100 --> 01:13:17.400
Now, at the risk of repeating myself,
what's the goddamn login?

832
01:13:22.100 --> 01:13:23.500
Don't fucking tell him.

833
01:13:26.500 --> 01:13:28.700
No! Don't! Don't!

834
01:13:31.700 --> 01:13:33.700
September 19.
September one-nine.

835
01:13:40.800 --> 01:13:42.800
Enough! September 19!

836
01:13:44.900 --> 01:13:45.900
Stop.

837
01:13:49.300 --> 01:13:50.400
September one-nine.

838
01:13:52.800 --> 01:13:54.400
Well, isn't that romantic?

839
01:13:58.500 --> 01:13:59.900
How do I disable it?

840
01:14:01.200 --> 01:14:02.500
Command F6.

841
01:14:14.500 --> 01:14:15.700
Now go touch it.

842
01:14:26.700 --> 01:14:28.000
Then I'll throw you.

843
01:14:36.500 --> 01:14:37.600
It's safe.

844
01:14:57.900 --> 01:14:59.600
Oh, will you look at that?

845
01:15:06.400 --> 01:15:07.800
Sonny.

846
01:15:08.400 --> 01:15:11.000
My brother, you don't need me.

847
01:15:11.800 --> 01:15:13.100
So I'll just go.

848
01:15:15.800 --> 01:15:16.900
He's right.

849
01:15:18.000 --> 01:15:19.300
We don't need him.

850
01:15:25.500 --> 01:15:26.500
Shit.

851
01:15:27.400 --> 01:15:28.900
It's still spinning.

852
01:15:30.200 --> 01:15:31.500
There's a manual shutdown.

853
01:15:31.600 --> 01:15:33.500
Then fucking disable it.

854
01:15:57.100 --> 01:15:58.400
Run!

855
01:16:20.500 --> 01:16:22.000
It's not mine.
Come on.

856
01:16:25.000 --> 01:16:27.200
All right. Okay, go.
Go, go, go.

857
01:16:38.200 --> 01:16:39.400
- Ready?
- Yeah.

858
01:16:53.500 --> 01:16:55.200
Here!

859
01:16:56.400 --> 01:16:57.500
Here.

860
01:17:04.800 --> 01:17:05.900
Take it.

861
01:17:40.700 --> 01:17:42.100
It feels petrified.

862
01:17:43.100 --> 01:17:44.500
What is it?

863
01:17:49.000 --> 01:17:50.900
I think it's a boundary.

864
01:17:51.700 --> 01:17:53.300
The time loop ends here.

865
01:17:56.100 --> 01:17:59.100
So only time inside the circle
has been looping?

866
01:18:24.200 --> 01:18:26.700
Hannah, there's a safe house
two blocks north.

867
01:18:26.800 --> 01:18:29.100
It's marked as contaminated. It's not.
I will meet you there.

868
01:18:29.200 --> 01:18:30.500
You're coming with me.

869
01:18:30.600 --> 01:18:32.500
No. I can't let Sonny take the ARQ.

870
01:18:32.500 --> 01:18:35.200
Renton, listen to me.
You can't go back inside.

871
01:18:35.300 --> 01:18:37.600
The ARQ is off.
If you die, you die forever.

872
01:18:37.700 --> 01:18:39.000
Go.

873
01:18:39.900 --> 01:18:41.200
I won't leave you.

874
01:18:53.100 --> 01:18:54.300
Hannah?

875
01:18:55.600 --> 01:18:56.800
Go, go, go!

876
01:19:05.100 --> 01:19:08.700
<i>? 'Twas in the moon of wintertime ?</i>

877
01:19:09.600 --> 01:19:12.700
<i>? When all the birds had fled ?</i>

878
01:19:12.800 --> 01:19:17.800
<i>? That mighty Gitchi Manitou
Sent angel choirs instead ?</i>

879
01:19:19.700 --> 01:19:21.500
You must recognize me.

880
01:19:22.800 --> 01:19:25.800
- He tortured me.
- Hey. Look at me.

881
01:19:25.900 --> 01:19:27.500
Listen, you're okay.

882
01:19:29.800 --> 01:19:32.900
<i>? Jesus your King is born ?</i>

883
01:19:33.600 --> 01:19:36.200
<i>? Jesus is born ?</i>

884
01:19:40.200 --> 01:19:42.100
Tell me you haven't forgotten.

885
01:20:29.900 --> 01:20:32.700
You're okay. You're okay.

886
01:20:32.800 --> 01:20:33.900
Okay.

887
01:20:37.800 --> 01:20:40.500
It's over. Okay? It's over.

888
01:20:42.100 --> 01:20:44.000
It's over. It's over.

889
01:20:49.900 --> 01:20:52.100
Sonny turned the ARQ back on.

890
01:20:52.100 --> 01:20:54.000
He must want the loop to reset.

891
01:20:54.100 --> 01:20:56.000
It's okay.
Come on.

892
01:20:56.100 --> 01:20:57.400
Come on.

893
01:21:49.300 --> 01:21:52.400
<i>ZMP fiver-Delta is in proximity.</i>

894
01:21:52.500 --> 01:21:53.800
<i>Drop time imminent.</i>

895
01:21:54.600 --> 01:21:56.300
Sonny called in ZMPs.

896
01:21:57.700 --> 01:21:59.100
Okay.

897
01:21:59.200 --> 01:22:02.400
We download everything.
Burn it all.

898
01:22:03.700 --> 01:22:05.100
There isn't time.

899
01:22:05.200 --> 01:22:06.900
Take the ARQ to the Bloc.

900
01:22:08.400 --> 01:22:09.700
Really?

901
01:22:11.700 --> 01:22:14.100
If there's no world left,
there's no hope for us.

902
01:22:20.600 --> 01:22:21.700
What?

903
01:22:24.000 --> 01:22:25.600
- What?
- Oh, my God.

904
01:22:28.800 --> 01:22:30.200
"Interruption."

905
01:22:31.700 --> 01:22:34.000
These time logs are the nine loops
we've gone through.

906
01:22:34.100 --> 01:22:37.000
Nine loops makes one sequence. There's...

907
01:22:38.600 --> 01:22:40.000
There's more sequences.

908
01:22:40.900 --> 01:22:43.900
So we've looped more than nine times?
How many?

909
01:22:45.300 --> 01:22:47.600
Ren, how many times have we loop...

910
01:22:54.200 --> 01:22:56.300
Thousands.
Maybe... maybe more.

911
01:22:59.100 --> 01:23:01.500
No, no, no, no, no, no.

912
01:23:01.600 --> 01:23:04.000
No, no, no, no, this can't be happening.

913
01:23:06.600 --> 01:23:08.800
The last timeline
in every sequence is broken.

914
01:23:08.900 --> 01:23:11.100
It's... it's when I shut down the ARQ
and Sonny rebooted it.

915
01:23:13.400 --> 01:23:15.200
When the ARQ reboots,
our memories must reset.

916
01:23:15.300 --> 01:23:17.300
That's why we don't remember the video.

917
01:23:17.400 --> 01:23:19.300
The video was recorded
in the last sequence.

918
01:23:19.400 --> 01:23:20.900
It was a message to us.

919
01:23:21.800 --> 01:23:23.500
And a ZMP stopped the message.

920
01:23:25.000 --> 01:23:26.200
They're in the house.

921
01:23:35.100 --> 01:23:36.200
Damn it!

922
01:23:37.200 --> 01:23:38.800
If Torus gets the ARQ...

923
01:23:40.400 --> 01:23:41.600
they win the war.

924
01:23:43.300 --> 01:23:44.900
We have to destroy it.

925
01:23:48.200 --> 01:23:49.400
God damn it!

926
01:24:05.900 --> 01:24:07.000
No.

927
01:24:09.900 --> 01:24:11.900
- What are you doing?
- We let the loop reset.

928
01:24:12.000 --> 01:24:13.900
We try again.

929
01:24:14.000 --> 01:24:15.600
We've tried already, thousands of times.

930
01:24:15.700 --> 01:24:18.000
We send a message to ourselves
in the next loop.

931
01:24:18.900 --> 01:24:22.200
Hannah, you were right.
We have to try.

932
01:24:25.600 --> 01:24:26.800
Hurry.

933
01:24:34.100 --> 01:24:37.100
Listen carefully. Torus...
Hannah!

934
01:24:37.200 --> 01:24:38.900
The message!

935
01:24:39.000 --> 01:24:40.000
Torus found you.

936
01:24:40.000 --> 01:24:42.200
Take the ARQ to the Bloc and trust Hannah!
